(O/'REVIEW.md').write_text('# V15 engineering experiment\n\nV15 is one adult-small local STEP retention pilot. It defines an intended M2x0.4 metal knob plus a separate jam nut, and records six discrete release and slider endpoint clearance checks. Its smooth cylinders stand for intended thread envelopes. They cannot prove real flank engagement, tightening, pullout or vibration resistance. Final grades, runout, gauges, coating, tools, torque and child access remain open. Native Fusion archives remain V10 and V14 remains the latest six-size candidate.\n\nThe child packing search uses unchanged V14 geometry. It ranks30625 boxes per size, checks a finite shortlist with actual solid intersections and stops at the first clear shortlisted endpoint. This is not a global optimisation or new folding-path pass. A failed initial interrupted search is retained separately; only final source-matched records support conclusions. Compare with fully retracted unfolded geometry, not only a nominal extension.\n\nThe72 retention load scenarios are reduced assumed-root rod calculations, not thread FE or a material or torque qualification. No physical comfort, autistic sensory acceptance, attenuation, outgoing music, heat, ageing, drops, folding life or market superiority pass exists. Sony pad and mount measurements remain deferred.\n\nRead both updated Word reports for the same revision-specific results and limits. Native Word pagination remains unverified; approximate page previews were checked. This is not a manufacturing release.\n')
